module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.admitted_call_edge_with_unrestricted_value_egress

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data admitted_call_edge_with_unrestricted_value_egress: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "admitted_call_edge_with_unrestricted_value_egress" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**AN ADMISSION LIST CONFINES THE CALL EDGE AND SAYS NOTHING ABOUT WHERE THE VALUE GOES NEXT, so a sealed constructor with an admitted caller is sealed only if that caller's own egress is closed** (INVALID STATE: a constructor is confined -- `sole_constructor`, or a mint carrying `admit_callers` -- and an enumerated caller is admitted to it, and the guarantee is then reported as `this state is unwritable outside the admission`. The admitted caller is an ordinary exported function that RETURNS the confined value, or a value containing it. In a language with NO MODULE-PRIVATE, which `.dag` is, that function is itself an unrestricted constructor for the same state: a foreign module imports the admitted caller rather than the mint, supplies whatever it likes, and obtains the confined value with no diagnostic. The admission list is a closed population only if its CLOSURE is closed, and nothing in the language says so. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the wall fires correctly on the direct route, so a probe aimed at the mint PASSES and reads as coverage; the escape is one import away and is invisible to any probe that only tests the direct edge. `admit_callers` on the admitted caller in turn does not fix it either -- it MOVES THE PROXY ONE HOP, because every helper that returns a value CARRYING the confined type is the same escape, and the cascade terminates only at functions that carry nothing outward. EVIDENCE, measured rather than argued (lively-ibex-812, gunbc#10934 landing and gunbc#10972 repair): `gunbc.fabric.fabric_m0_origin_readback` sealed `OriginReading` as a `sole_constructor` record and exported `witness_origin_reading` under `admit_callers` naming two witness wrappers. The direct-forgery probes all refused, and the merged claim read `structurally impossible outside the enumerated admission`. A foreign module importing the admitted wrapper test.claim.fabric_m0_commit_witness.witness_reading, passing a digest of its own choosing, and placing the result into `ManifestRead` COMPILED WITH 0 BLOCKING DIAGNOSTICS. In that same corpus the wrappers' own callers -- `object_reads`, `confirmed`, `reads_with_output`, `reads_with_receipt`, `reads_with_manifest` -- each returned a value carrying the reading, so the cascade would have needed every one of them sealed. RECOGNITION RULE: for any confined constructor, do not ask WHO MAY CALL IT; ask WHAT MAY LEAVE. Enumerate every exported function whose RETURN TYPE contains the confined type and that does not already REQUIRE one as a parameter -- each is an alternate mint. If that set is non-empty, the guarantee is about the direct edge only and must be reported that way. THE REPAIR, in preference order: remove the alternate mint entirely, so the confined type has exactly one constructor and the question does not arise; or close the egress -- every function returning a carrier must take the confined value as an input, so it propagates and never mints. The fabric-M0 instance took the first: the fixture mint was DELETED and its witnesses obtain readings through the real constructor, which required first repairing a `mock_response` that had never replayed so the hermetic route could execute at all. The residual egress is then statable exactly: the only zero-argument function returning a carrier is the sanctioned constructor itself, whose result a caller cannot aim. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the guarantee was reported at structural impossibility and the escape was found by a reviewer's probe, not by any mechanism. CEILING: structurally impossible, once egress closure is compiler-enforced rather than re-derived by hand. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY: either module-private declarations in `.dag`, so a fixture mint and its wrappers are unreachable from outside their module by construction; or an egress-closure check that, for a confined type, refuses any exported declaration whose return type contains it and whose parameters do not -- SUFFICIENT FOR deciding the alternate-mint set mechanically for EVERY confined type in the corpus, not for one carrier. Until one of those lands, terminality of an admission list is reviewed by hand and the class stays mitigatable. NOT THE DIGEST ROW: `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.subject_and_its_digest_as_independent_parameters` is about a value and a summary of it standing side by side with no join, and it cites this instance as its own repair's stumble. This row is about CONFINEMENT LEAKING THROUGH AN ADMITTED CALLER and applies to any sealed type, digest or not; folding the two would be the meaning fork DESIGN section 3 forbids.)",
    "**THE DEPLOY-TRANSITION LEASE HAD TWO OF THESE, AND THE WALL ON THE DIRECT EDGE IS EXACTLY WHY THEY WERE INVISIBLE** (INVALID STATE: `gunbc.deploy_transition_lease_store` `transition_lease_acquire_of(store, outcome)` took a `FileHoldAcquireOutcome` plus a store chosen in the SAME argument list and returned `TransitionLeaseAcquired { store, owner, generation }`, i.e. it MINTED the confined `TransitionLeaseHeld` carrier; and `gunbc.deploy_transition` `lease_acquisition_of(context, subject, holder, outcome)` took a caller-wrapped `TransitionLeaseAcquired` and returned a `TransitionGuard` for whatever context, subject and holder were named beside it. Both were exported, neither took the confined value as an input, and a foreign module reached each with one import. The direct-forgery probes PASSED throughout: `TransitionLeaseHeld` and `TransitionGuard` are `sole_constructor`, so the wall fired on their constructors and the seal witness read as coverage while the escape sat one import away. COMPOUNDING IT, the acquired arm of `FileHoldAcquired` is not keyed to the store or slot it came from -- `file_hold_ref(root, slot_key)` spells a directory, so a GENUINE acquire against store A slot X laundered into `TransitionLeaseHeld { store: B }`: two stores each believing they hold one lease. THE FIX TOOK THE REPAIR THIS ROW PREFERS FIRST, removing the alternate mints rather than sealing them: both folds are DELETED and their admitting arms are inline in the two functions that perform the effect -- `transition_lease_acquire` beside its own `file_hold_acquire(root: store.root, slot_key: transition_lease_slots.member, ...)`, with the slot key name-checked against the declaration, and `acquire_transition_lease` beside its own `transition_lease_acquire(store: context.lease, ...).` Each confined carrier is now produced exactly once, from the return value of the call that earned it; the public folds that remain are refusal-only and take no outcome-plus-store pair. `gunbc.deploy_transition` no longer even imports `TransitionLeaseAcquire`. a foreign module cannot import a function that does not exist, so the REDs are compile-census claims keyed on the missing callable (dag/test/claim/transition_lease_store_seal_witness.dag, laundering_route_is_gone): each route names the deleted fold in its own import list and the claim asserts exactly one blocking MissingExport on that name, so restoring either fold REDS the claim however much other noise the closure carries. A bare count delta would not have done: an earlier head of the same witness counted only \"more blocking rows than the baseline\", which closure noise satisfied. RECOGNITION RULE APPLIED RETROSPECTIVELY: these two folds were written as ordinary convenience renders over an outcome, which is what the fabric-M0 wrappers were too -- the warning this row already carries that \"an ordinary exported function that RETURNS the confined value\" is the escape, and that no probe aimed at the mint sees it. RUNG: unchanged, mitigatable -- a reviewer probing by hand found both, in two rounds, and no mechanism would have. The trigger stays the same capability (module-private declarations, or a compiler egress-closure check). (clever-dove-93, gunb-ai/gunbc#15105, lease cohort C-lease; found by the side chat at 462570c and by the operator review on 39e4935, not by any claim.)",
    "**THE SAME ESCAPE WITH NO ADMISSION LIST AT ALL: AN EXPORTED FOLD FROM AN EFFECT OUTCOME TO A SUCCESS** (INVALID STATE: an exported function takes an effect OUTCOME or READING value -- `FilesystemCreateNew`, `FileHoldReleaseOutcome`, `FilesystemWriteOutcome`, `CasOutcome` -- and returns a success-bearing value: a confined proof, a `Released`/`Stored`/`Committed` variant. The outcome types are unsealed and `.dag` has no private function, so a foreign module authors the outcome and obtains the success with no effect having run. The seal on the success value does not help when the success is a plain variant, and does not help when it is a sealed record, because the fold is the alternate mint. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the fold is written as an ordinary classification render, usually extracted so a hermetic witness can drive every arm, which is exactly why the witness itself becomes the foreign caller. RECOGNITION RULE: for every exported function, ask whether a PARAMETER's type is an effect outcome or reading and the RETURN contains a success the effect is supposed to earn; if so, inline the success arm beside the call whose return value it destructures, delete the fold, and keep at most a refusal-only classifier that returns no success. SWEEP, one lane, found four times (gunbc#15105, #15068, #15396, #15414) and swept into seven rows by jolly-hawk-60, plus an eighth found by sunny-swift-495 outside that sweep's module list, gunbc.host.managed_host_unit_hold `probe_hold_release_committed` (FileHoldReleaseOutcome -> ProbeHoldReleased, foreign caller test.claim.host.managed_host_unit_hold_witness; inlined beside file_hold_release_commit and DELETED here, held by the same keyed RED). The corpus-wide enumeration is by reviewer sweep only until the trigger below: (1) gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store `fabric_storage_put_from_create` -> FabricObjectStored, inlined and deleted in gunbc#15396 (silent-crab-631); (2) gunbc.compute.compute_producer_lease `compute_producer_lease_release_committed` -> ComputeProducerLeaseReleased, gunbc#15414 (sunny-swift-495); (3) extdeps.realization.materialization_store_local `store_publish_observation` -> StoreObjectPublished, gunbc#15414; (4) extdeps.realization.materialization_store_local `local_store_commit_released` -> LocalStoreCommit, gunbc#15414; (5) gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_request_record `attempt_request_binding_commit_of` -> RequestBindingCommitted, foreign caller test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_result_returned_witness, gunbc#15417 (royal-carp-132); (6) gunbc.deploy_transition_lease_store `transition_lease_release_committed` -> TransitionLeaseReleased, landed by gunbc#15105 and DELETED here; (7) gunbc.durable_cas_file_store `cas_outcome_from_create` -> CasCommitted, landed by gunbc#14944/#14972/#15068 with TWO foreign callers (test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_witness, five direct calls; and test.claim.approval_assertion_counter_wet_witness, which fed it a real write result) and DELETED here: the commit is the `Absent` arm of `cas_create_refusal` beside each `Filesystem.WriteCreateNew*` in `cas_commit_at`, and `cas_create_refusal` is refusal-only, returning `CasOutcome?` with none for a created file. Each deletion in this change is held by a keyed foreign-module RED asserting exactly one blocking MissingExport on the deleted name beside a lawful-path control (test.claim.outcome_laundering_seal_witness), the model being test.claim.transition_lease_store_seal_witness laundering_route_is_gone. WHAT WAS NOT DONE, AND WHY: `CasOutcome` was NOT sealed. `sole_constructor` is discarded on a coproduct right-hand side (class `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `modifier_accepted_on_a_shape_its_check_cannot_see`); a trial `type CasOutcome<T> sole_constructor` left test.claim.cas_outcome_seal_witness red and drew no violation from any of the ~35 modules that author its arms. The stale `gunbc#14447` trigger citation (it is the approve_ios PR, no seal PR exists) is corrected to the capability. Hermetic coverage of the success arm is lost for the same reason it was a defect: a real commit is exercised by test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_wet_witness and test.claim.approval_assertion_counter_wet_witness through file_compare_and_set, and the create-level classification arms that a real filesystem cannot produce (unrecognized kind, occupied with no readable winner) stay hermetic through the refusal-only fold. RUNG: the class is mitigatable, found by reviewer sweep. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the CAPABILITY of `sole_constructor` being honored on a coproduct right-hand side by the seed's parse/infer (recorded at `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `modifier_accepted_on_a_shape_its_check_cannot_see`); then `CasOutcome` and the other outcome types are sealed so only the effect function constructs them (construction, the class's ceiling). No lens is built meanwhile: it would be validation standing in for construction and deleted when the seal works. test.claim.cas_outcome_seal_witness stays as the expecting-red probe that greens when the capability lands. (witty-lynx-311, jolly-hawk-60's sweep.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
